<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:49:21 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The Observers</category><title>West Bank: settlers using drones to monitor Palestinians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261028-west-bank-settlers-using-drones-to-monitor-palestinians</link><description>
"We feel like we’re being watched all the time." In the occupied West Bank, Palestinian farmers are speaking out against the extensive use of drones by Israeli settlers and the Israeli military. According to activists and researchers, this practice is aimed, in part, at monitoring new Palestinian construction. In 2026, the Israeli government allocated a budget of 50 million shekels (over 14 million euros) to outposts and illegal settlements in the West Bank to fund so-called "security" equipment—which includes these drones.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c5fa79c-d2d4-11f1-958b-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/cisjordanie-vignette-dronesEN.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c5fa79c-d2d4-11f1-958b-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/cisjordanie-vignette-dronesEN.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4c5da24-d2d4-11f1-bfb5-fb9ace09e296</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:39:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marguerite Ipek LACROIX</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'No clear winner' from Israeli election, expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261028-no-clear-winner-from-israeli-election-expert-says</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, we focus on the results of the election in Israel. For analysis, we speak to Yossi Mekelberg, senior consulting fellow at Chatham House's Middle East and North Africa Programme. He tells us there is "no clear winner" from the country's pivotal vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed79bac8-d2cc-11f1-aa8e-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-23bfea15.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed79bac8-d2cc-11f1-aa8e-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-23bfea15.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb48bce8-d2be-11f1-8608-3f8c84ed87cf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:49:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli election: PM loses a significant number of seats since 2022 election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-pm-loses-a-significant-number-of-seats-since-2022-election</link><description>
Israel was counting votes on Wednesday after pivotal elections in which exit polls showed no clear winner. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s bloc appears to have lost a significant number of seats compared with the previous election in 2022. France 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley shares further insights. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c68de49c-d2c3-11f1-bf2b-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-903f4f39.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c68de49c-d2c3-11f1-bf2b-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-903f4f39.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73be25f2-d2c2-11f1-8c73-634728640b9f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:56:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli election: As votes are counted, no clear winner emerges</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-as-votes-are-counted-no-clear-winner-emerges</link><description>
Anxious Israelis watched election results take shape Wednesday after the highest turnout in over a quarter-century, as no clear winner emerged and weeks of negotiating could lie ahead for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and an array of opposition parties trying to unseat him. France 24 correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caf0c20c-d27d-11f1-8abe-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301069753352.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caf0c20c-d27d-11f1-8abe-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301069753352.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">902d37ba-d2bc-11f1-8290-cb8489b5f03c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:32:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Netanyahu edges closer to a majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-edges-closer-to-a-majority</link><description>
The final results are expected tonight or tomorrow morning. For now, the picture is looking increasingly favourable for Benjamin Netanyahu and his bloc, but the Israeli prime minister is still short of a clear victory, as he needs 61 seats to secure a parliamentary majority. He addressed his supporters at the National Congress Centre at around 3 a.m. local time. France 24’s Clovis Casali joins us live from Jerusalem with the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fc071c2-d2b7-11f1-b3c1-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-103209-103550-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fc071c2-d2b7-11f1-b3c1-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-103209-103550-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75028346-d2b7-11f1-a29d-e53fa7e154db</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:20:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Israeli election: 'Wishful thinking' for pro- and anti-Netanyahu parties?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261028-israeli-election-wishful-thinking-for-pro-and-anti-netanyahu-parties</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 28: Papers react to the ongoing election results in Israel. Next: Macklemore's Free Palestine tour is coming to Paris. Also: antidepressants don't work the way we thought. Finally: a sneak peek into boomer divorcées' dating lives.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/738802ce-d2b8-11f1-aa78-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-01a71472.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/738802ce-d2b8-11f1-aa78-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-01a71472.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28a97080-d2a4-11f1-a6c5-214657a457cd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:15:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Elitsa GADEVA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israelis await final election results as Netanyahu remains far from defeated</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israelis-await-final-election-results-as-netanyahu-remains-far-from-defeated</link><description>
Arab-led parties appear to have made a historic showing in the Israeli election, but it’s not clear if other opponents of Netanyahu's government would form a coalition with them for a majority in the next parliament. Issues around the Palestinians and their descendants remain incredibly sensitive in Israel.
 
France 24 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert shares further insights. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c57493c4-d2b6-11f1-8034-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a07f83f9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c57493c4-d2b6-11f1-8034-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a07f83f9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e140c784-d2b2-11f1-a0e7-0d8b2167ed7c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:12:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: The economic challenges ahead</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-the-economic-challenges-ahead</link><description>
Questions over the future of Israel’s economy are looming in the wake of the elections. With one of the highest costs of living in the region, and defence spending continuing to rise, households are facing growing financial pressure. Caitlin Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/badb3ed0-d2b2-11f1-8a6d-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101022-101222-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/badb3ed0-d2b2-11f1-8a6d-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101022-101222-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c02d00a8-d2b2-11f1-8d5e-dbb84a333bbe</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:43:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel election: There's no clear winner</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-there-s-no-clear-winner</link><description>
The path ahead remains uncertain in the Knesset in Jerusalem, as the Central Elections Committee continues to count the votes. With more than 60% of ballots tallied, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s camp is narrowly ahead of the opposition, but still short of a clear majority. 

These are still partial results and could change, meaning no clear winner has emerged so far. Both leading candidates for the prime minister’s office traded barbs in their respective speeches after polls closed. Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae9d138-d2b1-11f1-bfca-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-100155-100340-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae9d138-d2b1-11f1-bfca-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-100155-100340-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4096c2a8-d2b1-11f1-8133-21d823290669</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:40:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Netanyahu and Eisenkot both pledge to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israel-netanyahu-and-eisenkot-both-pledge-to-form-government</link><description>
 🗳️ Both Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin #Netanyahu and rival Gadi #Eisenkot pledged to form a government as the two are projected to finish neck and neck in #Israel's critical election Tuesday. 
 
Exit polls show both blocs falling short of a parliamentary majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e33c442-d2b0-11f1-9449-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/title-5.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e33c442-d2b0-11f1-9449-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/title-5.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e5d8e03c-d2ae-11f1-8882-7f054befa3c0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:06:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel election: Netanyahu and Eisenkot battle to form government after deadlock</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-record-turnout-netanyahu-eisenkot-deadlock</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and rival Gadi Eisenkot on Wednesday both pledged to form a government after an election left neither bloc with a parliamentary majority. Record voter turnout followed a divisive campaign dominated by the October 7, 2023 attack, while Arab Israeli parties made significant gains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0844dc0-d24e-11f1-bac3-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T201655Z-2088081210-RC2WBOANCXWD-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0844dc0-d24e-11f1-bac3-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T201655Z-2088081210-RC2WBOANCXWD-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df034636-d258-11f1-b9bc-e9013cf76742</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:58:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0844dc0-d24e-11f1-bac3-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T201655Z-2088081210-RC2WBOANCXWD-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg">© Shir Torem, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: First exit polls show no clear winner, Arab parties make gains</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-israel-first-exit-polls-show-no-clear-winner-arab-parties-make-gains</link><description>
Exit polls on Tuesday showed that the opposition bloc led by Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot gained a narrow edge over Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud bloc in the Knesset. 
 
Likud, however, was projected to be the largest single party in the Israeli parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42df8b48-d24e-11f1-a8a6-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Israel-elex-results-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42df8b48-d24e-11f1-a8a6-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Israel-elex-results-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">539b2cc6-d24e-11f1-be4f-5d1034af3744</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:41:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Bibi's moment of truth: Israel votes in first general election since October 7 attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261027-bibi-s-moment-of-truth-israel-votes-in-first-general-election-since-october-7</link><description>
The turnout tells the tale. Israelis are casting ballots in their largest numbers in decades in the first general election since the October 7 attacks of 2023. The vote is seen as a referendum on the bloodiest day in the nation's history. But more broadly, what kind of Israel do citizens want? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec4db540-d237-11f1-89c8-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/Portraits-politiques-en-diptyque-%C3%A9ditorial.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec4db540-d237-11f1-89c8-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/Portraits-politiques-en-diptyque-%C3%A9ditorial.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5662ef6-d236-11f1-985f-1d6731835462</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:26:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu govt has 'attacked' Israeli judicial system, Supreme Court and democratic institutions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-govt-has-attacked-israeli-judicial-system-supreme-court-and-democratic-institutions</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Alain Greilsammer, Professor of Political Science at Bar-Ilan University in Tel Aviv. In the wake of the October 7 attacks, regional tensions with Iran, and deepening domestic divisions, Greilsammer argues that the election will be fundamentally shaped by concerns over democratic accountability, judicial independence and the unequal distribution of civic obligations. He warns Netanyahu’s policies risk transforming Israel into “something like an authoritarian or non-democratic state.” He suggests that Israel’s Arab political parties could play a decisive role in determining the election’s outcome. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44b94f32-d215-11f1-870d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-130828-131530-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44b94f32-d215-11f1-870d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-130828-131530-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a9e2b0c-d215-11f1-bbd3-8db6a196f0d8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:44:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ibrahim Abu Ahmad on Israeli election: 'Crucial for Arab citizens to have ally in Jewish community'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-ibrahim-abu-ahmad-on-israeli-election-crucial-for-arab-citizens-to-have-ally-in-jewish-community</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ibrahim Abu Ahmad, Author, Palestinian Israeli political and peace activist and Head of Social Media for Israel's left-wing Democrats. “Currently, the sentiment in Israel is built around fear and trauma,” explains Ahmad. His most striking observation concerns the apparent contradiction between political leadership and public sentiment: “Many want to see an Arab-Jewish coalition. It's the leadership that is afraid to say it.” Ultimately, he moves beyond conventional electoral calculations to frame Arab-Jewish partnership as a question of democratic survival.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b957c3a8-d235-11f1-be1e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-160657-162025-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b957c3a8-d235-11f1-be1e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-160657-162025-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf66238e-d235-11f1-a9a7-358d90d616ad</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:59:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli elections a 'referendum' on Netanyahu, security and whether Israel will 'remain a democracy'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-elections-a-referendum-on-netanyahu-security-and-whether-israel-will-remain-a-democracy</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ron Gerlitz, CEO of aChord Center at Hebrew University, an Israeli organization specialising in the social psychology of intergroup relations. “The main issue in this election is the fight for Israeli democracy,” explains Gerlitz. And beneath the struggle over democratic institutions lies the erosion of Benjamin Netanyahu's longstanding association with national security. Gerlitz also examines the psychological foundations of Netanyahu's enduring support, the influence of conspiracy narratives, the electoral significance of Arab parties and the uncertain future of the two-state solution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/029a5de6-d227-11f1-88b5-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-151044-152521-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/029a5de6-d227-11f1-88b5-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-151044-152521-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08356f48-d227-11f1-b360-5985141447d7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:34:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israelis vote in a tense election: What's at stake?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-a-tense-election-what-s-at-stake</link><description>
Israelis were voting Tuesday (October 27) in a tense national election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership since the Hamas-led Oct. 7, 2023, attack on Israel and the wars that have since shaken the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e9752f2-d226-11f1-b354-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-163137-163342-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e9752f2-d226-11f1-b354-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-163137-163342-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">745b18ea-d226-11f1-8986-e734320f3c2e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:59:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel elections: voter turnout reaches 55% by 4pm local time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-elections-voter-turnout-reaches-55-by-4pm-local-time</link><description>
Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on veteran right-wing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. FRANCE24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6478d3e-d226-11f1-8753-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7dc5f0be.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6478d3e-d226-11f1-8753-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7dc5f0be.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7f5f6cc-d225-11f1-9ba7-a50718b24c28</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:52:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel votes in decisive election: What happens after polls close?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-israel-s-unique-political-system-what-happens-after-polls-close</link><description>
Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. Details by FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Angela Diffley.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26988dbe-d216-11f1-add4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b7810f8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26988dbe-d216-11f1-add4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b7810f8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2ccdb20-d211-11f1-a5c3-171811636c23</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:55:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Turnout high as Israeli voters deliver verdict on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/turnout-high-as-israeli-voters-deliver-verdict-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. Former FRANCE 24 correspondent, Irris Makler, tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a21d00-d212-11f1-a0b4-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-150546-151042-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a21d00-d212-11f1-a0b4-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-150546-151042-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9aac309c-d212-11f1-ae4b-112991d1df27</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:45:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Netanyahu supporters gather as PM votes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes</link><description>
Supporters of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gathered outside a polling station where the leader was voting on Tuesday. This is Israel's first election since the October7, 2023 Hamas attack and is seen as a referendum on Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29a441e-d213-11f1-b65d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-174.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29a441e-d213-11f1-b65d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-174.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f53db742-d212-11f1-8496-c5c7d9541c07</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:37:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Israeli election: A referendum on 'Bibi' Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu</link><description>
